{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"3364da81f27f1ee897cace66cf9e75f0d6da96e3e00b40688eca182060e8e6df","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_d5425e4ed60d0e0fa29b77bfd3a7d3ec0890507672121bb29ee9bd109707af9a","overall_assessment":"The paper is clearly written and well-organized, with a logical flow from conceptual motivation to technical implementation and experimental validation. The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined, and the algorithmic presentation is precise. The visual aids are supported by detailed captions and a readable table, effectively communicating the experimental setup and results.","paper_id":"ByvJuTigl","paper_identity_sha256":"8b6d11b0eca8e77b4a891a84948e75b0deeea4183c5f5eb32540dbb501069a54","prompt_identity_sha256":"d60c7523e16f7787e3e2113e86202d5f1dff85f35774a30a891672ab1897aa2d","raw_response_sha256":"78abe7e8ed9568e32bb42c19f9aefc9c8989a919f0e51f7ebb757d92c5c0ddea","request_identity_sha256":"d594a0d8be2c0e25888212f3d2f5e8a277f398530ac57376e928e32d105aa3ae","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"312e1bf2eaae4236232941ece8b032cb4a580ba63c99589dd8e4e654194f1754","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037","SRC-038"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured, moving logically from the conceptual motivation of combining algorithms and machine learning to the specific technical implementation of the End-to-End Learnable Histogram Filter (E2E-HF). The terminology is precise, with key concepts such as 'belief,' 'motion model,' and 'measurement model' clearly defined in the preliminaries and used consistently throughout. The algorithmic presentation is clear, particularly in Section 5, where the differentiable implementation of the histogram filter is broken down into belief, prediction, and measurement update steps. The use of vector and matrix operations to describe the filter's components aids in understanding the computational aspects. The experimental section is well-organized, clearly stating the problem, the methods compared, and the results, with a logical flow from data efficiency to end-to-end performance and unsupervised learning.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. The paper introduces the belief as a vector b, the motion model as a function g, and the measurement model as a function h, and these symbols are used consistently in the subsequent equations. The derivation of the prediction step as a convolution and the measurement update as an element-wise multiplication is clearly explained, with the necessary assumptions (e.g., local and consistent motion) stated. The learning objectives for supervised and unsupervised learning are presented with clear definitions of the variables involved, such as the subsequence length C and the prediction horizon D. The notation for the basis vector e^(i) is also clearly defined, aiding in the understanding of the loss functions.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-015","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-029","SRC-033","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The visual aids are supported by detailed and informative captions. Figure 1 provides a high-level overview of the E2E-HF, clearly indicating which components are learned and which are given. Figure 3 offers a more detailed view of the filter's architecture, with a caption that explains the roles of the motion and measurement models. The captions for Figures 4, 5, 6, and 7 are descriptive, specifying the tasks, metrics, and conditions under which the results are shown. Table 1 is readable and clearly presents the test performance of different methods on the drone task, with columns for MSE, accuracy of state estimation, and accuracy of observation prediction. The textual descriptions of the figures and tables in the main text are consistent with the captions, aiding in the interpretation of the results.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"e13eeba219fa912a229878dbcab1dd2ae8236d35caee0ec671ac4def9b2fbcc4","paper_id":"ByvJuTigl","paper_ordinal":83,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"78abe7e8ed9568e32bb42c19f9aefc9c8989a919f0e51f7ebb757d92c5c0ddea","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"ByvJuTigl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"83030474d762ceb90b667267e0f3554503ea6673b6d652cfcb9ad6b73bee5818","request_identity_sha256":"d594a0d8be2c0e25888212f3d2f5e8a277f398530ac57376e928e32d105aa3ae","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1201,"prompt_tokens":18176,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19377},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"d594a0d8be2c0e25888212f3d2f5e8a277f398530ac57376e928e32d105aa3ae","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}